        "shorts"
      ],
      "script": "My neighbor let his dog cross onto my lawn every morning and never picked up what followed. I asked twice, then installed a bright orange motion sprinkler aimed only at my grass. The next morning, his dog crossed onto my lawn, the sprinkler clicked on, and both of them retreated very quickly. He complained to the HOA that I was “harassing” his pet and attached a photo as proof. At the hearing, I enlarged the photo he submitted. It showed the sprinkler entirely inside my property line, plus his dog standing off-leash on my lawn beside an untouched waste bag dispenser. Our rules allow sprinklers, but they fine owners for off-leash dogs and uncollected waste. The board dismissed his complaint and issued him two violations from his own evidence. He now walks on the opposite sidewalk carrying three bags. The sprinkler has not had another customer.",
