    {
      "subreddit": "entitledparents",
      "slug": "pickup-line-rule-backfired",
      "title": "The Pickup Rule Sent A Line Cutter To The Back",
      "hashtags": [
        "entitledparents",
        "schoolpickup",
        "parent",
        "maliciouscompliance",
        "karma",
        "rules",
        "storytime",
        "shorts"
      ],
      "script": "I volunteer at my daughter's elementary school pickup, where every car waits in one marked line. One parent cut around twenty waiting cars, stopped at the front cone, and held up an expired pickup placard. When I asked her to rejoin the line, she leaned on the horn and demanded I enforce the rules exactly. So I did. The written procedure says expired placards require an in-person ID check at the front office before a child can be released. I radioed the front office, logged her plate, and sent her to the visitor lane. She argued long enough for every car she had passed to collect their kids and leave. When she finally reached the curb, the principal handed her a new placard and a copy of the procedure she had quoted at me. The next afternoon she arrived early, joined the back, and kept both hands off the horn.",
